# NestJS & Prisma Server Roo Code Rules

## Architecture & Code Style
1. NestJS Standards: Follow modular architecture (Controller -> Service -> Repository/Prisma). Keep business logic in Services and routing/request handling in Controllers.
2. DTO & Validation: Always define DTOs for request payloads using `class-validator` and `class-transformer`. Enforce strict TypeScript typing (avoid `any`).
3. Prisma ORM: Place database access methods inside services. Ensure queries respect `prisma/schema.prisma`.

## Token & Cost Optimization
1. Targeted Diffs: Modify only the specific lines or methods needed. Never rewrite entire files or unchanged modules.
2. Concise Output: Provide direct, minimal code edits and answers. Avoid conversational filler or introductions.
3. Primary Scope: Focus file scans strictly within `src/` and `prisma/`. Do not inspect `deploy/`, `topik_data/`, or `photos/` unless explicitly instructed.

## Terminal & Execution
1. Minimal Commands: Do not execute `npm run build` or `nest start` after minor code edits. Run `npx prisma generate` only when `prisma/schema.prisma` is modified.
2. Efficient Debugging: Carefully analyze NestJS Dependency Injection (DI) errors or Prisma query exceptions from the error stack trace before attempting code edits.